# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in your FootyStats API key.
# `.env` is ignored by git: the key must never be committed, printed or logged.
# Key: https://footystats.org -> your account -> API.
#
# FootyStats is the only source of real data (teams, calendars, results, odds). The data are
# licensed to you as the key holder and this repository is PUBLIC, so they are fetched at
# runtime with YOUR key and stored only on your machine (data/ is git-ignored): nothing is
# ever published to GitHub. `avvia.bat` / `avvia.command` read this file, download the data and
# synchronise the team dictionary (config/teams_2026_27.json) with FootyStats before opening
# the dashboard. Without a key there are no real data: the dashboard never shows simulated
# matches as if they were real.
#
# Streamlit Community Cloud: do NOT upload a .env file. Put the key in the app settings,
# "Secrets" (Settings -> Secrets), as one line:
#   FOOTYSTATS_API_KEY = "your-key"
# The app reads it at runtime and downloads the data into its own (temporary) disk.
#
# On footystats.org add the competitions to your account ("Choose leagues"): the API refuses
# the data of a league that is not chosen ("League is not chosen by the user"), so a
# competition whose league is missing is skipped (the others are still downloaded). Leagues
# needed for all 13 configured competitions (the `footystats_name` column of
# config/competitions.toml):
#   Italy Serie C Group A, Italy Serie C Group B, Italy Serie C Group C, Italy Serie B,
#   Italy Serie D Group A, Italy Serie D Group B, Italy Serie D Group C,
#   Italy Serie D Group D, Italy Serie D Group E, Italy Serie D Group F,
#   Italy Serie D Group G, Italy Serie D Group H, Italy Serie D Group I
# FootyStats plans cap the number of chosen leagues: if you cannot add them all,
# narrow the run with `--competitions` (e.g. A B C SB).
FOOTYSTATS_API_KEY=
